  Slug: dedicated-delver
  DisplayName: Dedicated Delver
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/background.svg
  Description: 'Filled with predators, pitfalls, and other perils, the Darklands
    rightfully scares off most travelers. Not you! Whether you''re a veteran Darklands
    caravanner, a cartographer seeking safer paths through dangerous territory, or
    just a spelunker who loves to escape the surface and hear the caverns sing, you''re
    adept at navigating underground obstacles and finding your way back to civilization.
    Clan Tolorr specializes more in studying the past than extracting it from dangerous
    areas. Its leader, Arghan Tolorr, was an avid explorer in his youth, and he''s
    begun an initiative to befriend, recruit, and train subterranean daredevils who
    can extract relics responsibly. You''re one of his candidates for this pilot
    program. Helping administrate recruits is Ria, a gnome curator and close Tolorr
    confidante who helped arrange your travel to Highhelm. Choose two attribute boosts.
    One must be to Strength or Dexterity , and one is a free attribute boost. You''re
    trained in either the Athletics skill or the Survival skill, and you''re trained
    in the Cave Lore skill. If you selected Athletics, you gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Combat
    Climber] skill feat. If you chose Survival, you gain the Terrain Expertise (Underground)
    skill feat. Connection: Ria, an oread gnome curator who studies rivethun traditions
    Reputation Points: +0'
